WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.440
Etsy is slowly turning into slop.
It was the place for handcrafted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.200
high quality products, with&nbsp;
over 7 million sellers.&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.760
But now, many of those sellers…&nbsp;
aren’t making handmade stuff.&nbsp;

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:20.800
If you search for artwork, crochet patterns,&nbsp;
armor, or rugs, you'll find AI art everywhere.&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.560
Digital products spat out by ChatGPT… some&nbsp;
of them stealing from actual sellers on Etsy.&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.960
The share price is down 80%,&nbsp;
Buyers are down. Sellers are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:38.400
down. Growth last year was just 2.6 percent.
Etsy's own AI decides what you see, and what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.640
gets removed. And right now, it's removing&nbsp;
the actual sellers, whose work was stolen.&nbsp;

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:52.240
Yet, Etsy's CEO said "You couldn't run Etsy&nbsp;
without AI." And before that, he said "Being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.960
good doesn't cut the mustard."
What on earth happened to Etsy?&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:12.000
When did Etsy turn to AI slop?
If you’re unfamiliar, Etsy is an ecommerce space&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:19.200
for selling handmade items, vintage items, and&nbsp;
craft supplies. Well, that’s what it used to be.&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.360
Its original mission was to “keep&nbsp;
commerce human,” and that quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.600
drew in many creative entrepreneurs&nbsp;
who could sell something more personal.&nbsp;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:33.920
They were more expensive, but you were supporting&nbsp;
a local artist or small business. Like you were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:39.040
buying from someone in your neighborhood.
Someone’s own handmade art, or maybe something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.440
wooden with a personal engraving,&nbsp;
or even a medieval knight’s helmet.&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.640
It felt like you were buying from someone who&nbsp;
loved their craft, and was really good at it.&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:54.400
To be clear, there are still a ton of fantastic&nbsp;
products made by great sellers on Etsy.&nbsp;

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.680
But things have changed a&nbsp;
lot in the past few years.&nbsp;

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:03.040
The pool of authentic sellers… is&nbsp;
shrinking. Because Etsy has implicitly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.280
favored another type of seller.
Ironically, selling handmade stuff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:13.760
is now one of the hardest things to do on Etsy.
A search for crochet patterns will pull dozens of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:21.600
AI-generated images ahead of handcrafted images.
Etsy's policy allows AI-generated content,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:28.720
and we’ll go more into that, don’t you worry.
But these patterns cost $2 to $10 and are meant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.360
to instruct the buyer on how to create&nbsp;
the image featured on the store page.&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.480
But with dozens of these AI images&nbsp;
as the top results, many learners new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:45.120
to crocheting are scammed. Because… it’s&nbsp;
AI. Of course it’s not going to be right.&nbsp;

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.680
That’s not shade at the buyers, not&nbsp;
everyone has a strong eye for AI.&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.560
But these stores have hundreds, and&nbsp;
some even thousands, of sales and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.280
at the same time, reviews warning others&nbsp;
not to fall into the scam like they had.&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.000
“The pattern looks nothing like the&nbsp;
picture that advertised the pattern.”&nbsp;

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.520
“The image is an AI-generated image, and I&nbsp;
will never purchase from this seller again.”&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.600
Some mix authentic pictures with&nbsp;
AI images to avoid suspicion.&nbsp;

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.080
“The first picture in the&nbsp;
listing is what makes you want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:21.600
to buy the pattern, as it’s AI-generated.”
It goes far beyond crochet patterns though.&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.640
“Forced to buy from Amazon and Ebay&nbsp;
because AI slop has ruined etsy.”&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.120
Of course, these sellers will also just&nbsp;
lie about the condition of the products.&nbsp;

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:38.000
Oh that’s if you even get the product by the way.
“Shops may use AI-generated images that claim to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.280
show handmade or custom items. The product may&nbsp;
not even exist. By the time you realize you’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.920
purchased from a fake Etsy shop, the seller&nbsp;
has likely removed it from the platform,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:51.680
potentially leaving you out of pocket&nbsp;
and vulnerable to identity theft with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:56.480
limited options for recourse.”
These scams are called Vibescams.&nbsp;

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:01.760
When Etsy was asked for a statement, they&nbsp;
said: “We want our buyers to know we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:06.000
their backs — so in the rare case that&nbsp;
a shopper receives an item that does not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:10.480
match the listing image or description, they&nbsp;
can open a case and receive a full refund&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:15.920
through our Purchase Protection Program.”
Yeah… “very, super rare occasion,” guys.&nbsp;

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:19.840
But this might not even be the worst&nbsp;
thing these resellers have done.&nbsp;

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.280
You know that amazing feeling&nbsp;
of a fresh, new Macbook?&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.600
One that’s still in top shape, still&nbsp;
buttery smooth and highly responsive?&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.960
But, the native systems aren't always the&nbsp;
best to maintain this, especially on Mac.&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:39.280
