Some will blatantly reuse images from sellers on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:10.320
Etsy, and sell them on eBay or other platforms.
“I am a designer. My product has been stolen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:16.240
and the vendor has used AI to modify my image.&nbsp;
They are selling it on eBay. My sales for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:21.760
this product have stopped, as the AI version&nbsp;
looks appealing, and theirs have soared! But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:27.200
eBay doesn't accept that it has infringed my IP&nbsp;
rights! Help!! I'm really scared she's just going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.680
to go through my whole catalogue. She's&nbsp;
adding multiple new patterns every day.”&nbsp;

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.760
I feel so bad for this seller.&nbsp;
But sadly, there’s something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:42.080
Etsy has done, which makes this even worse.
Authentic sellers are now competing to rank&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:47.200
together with stores that copied their designs.
This has caused some sellers who started before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.440
the AI boom to experience&nbsp;
a sharp decline in sales.&nbsp;

00:06:51.440 --> 00:07:17.760
But this is just the tip of the iceberg.
These videos, are everywhere.&nbsp;

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:24.880
The Etsy market, is flooded with these listings.
They just assume because it’s on Etsy… buyers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.640
believe that they are supporting a&nbsp;
local artist, especially those who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:36.000
lack the discernment to tell it’s fake.
And boy, these get way, WAY worse.&nbsp;

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:13.440
It’s not just for AI either,&nbsp;
but also dropshipping.&nbsp;

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:31.760
Dropshipping isn’t inherently bad,&nbsp;
but on Etsy? The place for hand-made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:36.960
products? It all feels a bit weird.
Mass-produced items on AliExpress or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:41.760
Temu are sold as handmade products&nbsp;
for double or quadruple the price.&nbsp;

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:44.000
What happened?
What decisions and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:57.280
changes caused Etsy to get so bad?
And, is all of it backfiring?&nbsp;

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:04.240
In 2012, Etsy made a commitment by becoming a&nbsp;
Certified B Corporation: "We believe that business&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:10.960
has a higher social purpose beyond simply profit."
This is basically a for-profit business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:15.040
but with higher standards for&nbsp;
social and environmental impact.&nbsp;

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:20.080
But soon, Etsy made a change.
In 2013, in an announcement made by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:25.440
CEO Dickerson, it now allowed sellers to have as&nbsp;
many people as they needed to run their business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:29.760
as well as have someone else ship their&nbsp;
goods, and even have manufacturing partners.&nbsp;

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:33.920
This might sound awful, but… I&nbsp;
don’t think this was a bad change.&nbsp;

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:38.800
You can still make a design, an innovation,&nbsp;
a style, and partner with someone to produce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:42.240
more of it to meet demand.
Etsy simply couldn't scale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:47.840
if every seller had to make every product by&nbsp;
hand. Working with production partners can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:52.560
still produce something unique, provided&nbsp;
the original idea belongs to the seller.&nbsp;

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:57.040
Not everyone was thrilled with this:&nbsp;
“Their moniker is, you know, a place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:04.240
to buy handmade. It doesn't say a place to buy&nbsp;
factory-made,” and “It started out to be a place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:10.640
where you could get something special, something&nbsp;
one-of-a-kind, something made by a human being.”&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:15.120
This change, would inevitably lead to&nbsp;
a gradual shift in sellers on Etsy.&nbsp;

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:21.171
By 2015, when it wanted to go public,&nbsp;
Dickerson could no longer ignore the concerns.&nbsp;

00:10:21.171 --> 00:10:23.920
[Chad Dickerson, CEO, Etsy]: "I have heard&nbsp;
concerns that by allowing our sellers to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:28.800
partner with responsible manufacturers,&nbsp;
we are diluting our handmade ethos."&nbsp;

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:35.680
He insisted that “the website still values&nbsp;
craftsmanship”, but not everyone was convinced.&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:40.240
"The decision to allow manufactured&nbsp;
products was one to improve Etsy’s revenue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:46.240
but it affected Etsy artisans detrimentally."
“They fundamentally changed the purpose of Etsy.”&nbsp;

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:50.720
“To stay true to my handmade ethos,&nbsp;
I had to move my business elsewhere.”&nbsp;

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:56.880
Then, Josh Silverman joined Etsy's board&nbsp;
in 2016 and began to make some changes.&nbsp;

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.840
Just, not the ones sellers were hoping for.
The board fired Dickerson and installed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:06.560
Silverman as CEO instead.
22% of the workforce would be cut,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:13.040
about 230 people. Granted, according to Etsy,&nbsp;
many of these roles were in middle management.&nbsp;

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:17.520
Etsy employees signed a petition, with&nbsp;
multiple demands, asking the company to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:21.680
"Stand for more than just Profits"
But it seems like only one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:26.000
the demands was ever met.
And, to add insult to injury,&nbsp;

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:29.600
Later, in November, Silverman&nbsp;
dropped the B Corporation label.&nbsp;

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:35.040
“The company had the best of intentions,&nbsp;
but wasn't great at tying that to impact....&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:40.400
Being good doesn't cut the mustard."
“Etsy has lost their identity. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:45.760
started for makers and other creatives,&nbsp;
and now is more of an online strip mall.”&nbsp;

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:50.240
But ironically, around this&nbsp;
time, Etsy had its big break.&nbsp;

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:54.240
The pandemic sent everyone home...&nbsp;
people started shopping online,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:58.160
while others started side hustles.
And Etsy was built for this.&nbsp;

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:02.160
The total value of everything sold on&nbsp;
Etsy jumped from about $5 billion in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:10.080
2019 to $12.2 billion in 2021. Its stock&nbsp;
price also skyrocketed to $274 per share.&nbsp;

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:14.880
It took advantage of cheap borrowing&nbsp;
and began expanding aggressively.&nbsp;

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:21.600
Within weeks, it spent nearly $2 billion. It&nbsp;
acquired Depop for $1.625 billion on June 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:27.040
then Elo7 for $217 million on June 28.
Lots of money spent in less than a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:31.200
month. But debt was cheap.
With all this new demand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:37.520
Etsy saw a new opportunity.
The transaction fee increased from 3.5% to 5%.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:42.880
Sellers using Offsite Ads could also&nbsp;
be charged an additional 12% to 15%.&nbsp;

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:46.800
Those who didn't offer free shipping&nbsp;
became less visible in search results.&nbsp;

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:52.240
Then Etsy raised the transaction&nbsp;
fee again, from 5% to 6.5%.&nbsp;

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:57.760
It became so much that in April 2022,&nbsp;
over 20,000 sellers went on strike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:02.320
setting their stores to “vacation mode”.
In response, Etsy committed to investing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:07.600
more into trust and safety, and to adding&nbsp;
50 human agents to enforce policies better.&nbsp;

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:13.680
But… in the end, the protest changed nothing.
Etsy kept the higher fees and things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:17.520
soon got much worse.
So, when exactly did Etsy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:25.600
become flooded with AI slop?
And, is Etsy dying?&nbsp;

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:36.240
If you’ve made it this far, you might like our&nbsp;
videos, so consider subscribing! We’re trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:40.880
reach a million, and need your help. Thanks
Let’s take a look at the data.&nbsp;

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:48.720
From 2023 to 2025, Etsy has lost 5.5 million&nbsp;
active buyers and one million habitual buyers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:55.120
The total value of everything sold on Etsy has&nbsp;
fallen from $12.1 billion to $10.5 billion.&nbsp;

00:13:55.120 --> 00:14:02.320
And this isn’t too surprising given the state&nbsp;
of Etsy today, and one big policy they changed.&nbsp;

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:06.640
The meaning of handcrafted&nbsp;
items has changed once again.&nbsp;

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:14.320
AI is now considered creative and has a dedicated&nbsp;
category for it: “seller-prompted AI creation.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:20.000
Sellers just have to disclose this.
This sounds ok if it’s enforced.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:24.640
Because plenty just don’t disclose it.
Buyers have to painstakingly go through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:29.920
every picture to get to something real.
But not only do many sellers use AI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:36.000
Etsy's platform uses AI too.
AI is now the algorithm. It uses LLMs to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:40.800
deliver search results and recommendations.
But based on what we’ve seen recently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:46.080
it sure seems like these favor bright,&nbsp;
clickable AI images over the genuine listings.&nbsp;

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:52.640
At the same time, AI also polices the products.
To be clear, LLMs can be an amazing tool to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:56.560
identify scams and fraud, and&nbsp;
remove AI content. It’s making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.560 --> 00:15:02.880
a huge difference on YouTube at the moment.
But, it might be doing the opposite on Etsy.&nbsp;

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:07.440
Not only does it leave up stolen listings,&nbsp;
but it’s now flagging the original,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:14.160
authentic sellers, whose work has been stolen.
And a lot of the time, it can’t be appealed.&nbsp;

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:19.680
“My shop (was suspended, I guess because&nbsp;
some of my bestsellers photos were stolen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:25.360
by Chinese companies with deleted watermarks&nbsp;
on them. I had over 30000 sales and started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:30.960
my Etsy shop in 2017. I filled an appeal and&nbsp;
attached photos and video files showing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:38.160
my items are handmade. Unfortunately my appeal&nbsp;
was automatically closed in less than 3 minutes.”&nbsp;

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:43.120
“Hi, etsy has suspended my account after&nbsp;
suspending 3 of my listings for violating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:49.600
etsys creativity policy. Everything I produce&nbsp;
is handmade and of my own design. My designs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:55.520
and photos are currently being stolen by Chinese&nbsp;
wholesale websites such as temu, shein, Ali baba&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.520 --> 00:16:01.920
and Ali express. I have contacted etsy support&nbsp;
numerous times, and this morning I woke up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:08.640
my shop being suspended. I have filed an appeal&nbsp;
but have lost so much hope and trust in etsy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:16.000
I'm worried this is the end of my etsy shop.&nbsp;
I've sold over 70,000 products with over 14,000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:23.360
positive reviews with an average rating of 4.9”.
And a massive, more recent change by Etsy makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:26.160
this more interesting.
Before, their policy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:32.480
gave room for using templated designs or&nbsp;
patterns, but now that has been deleted.&nbsp;

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:37.040
Every item now has to be “based&nbsp;
on a seller’s original design”.&nbsp;

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:42.640
So what counts as unoriginal?
Sellers who use licensed design bundles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:47.760
STL files, or pre-made AI prompt&nbsp;
packs instead of creating their own.&nbsp;

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:51.920
But, in reality, this doesn’t&nbsp;
actually hit AI products.&nbsp;

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:58.320
In fact, it really hits drop shippers and even&nbsp;
some genuine sellers who legally licensed STL&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:04.080
files or designs. If you come with your own&nbsp;
prompts, that’s technically “based on your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.800
own design”.
Ironic.&nbsp;

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:10.320
So, is Etsy dying?
Well, some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:15.920
company's biggest bets... haven't paid off.
Those Covid acquisitions led to over $1.1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:19.280
billion in write-downs.
But Etsy's advertising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:26.160
revenue actually increased in early 2026,&nbsp;
bringing in an additional $14.4 million.&nbsp;

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:31.680
Sellers are now paying more for each click.
But, overall growth has slowed dramatically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:38.400
falling to just 2.6% growth in 2025.
When growth is that low, it shows a plateau.&nbsp;

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:42.320
Etsy is squeezing those already on&nbsp;
the platform, but it seems to me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:47.200
that buyers, and sellers, are leaving.
Those who care about handcrafted stuff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:53.600
have realized Etsy has become a worse Amazon.
And in a few years, I think Etsy is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:59.120
to pay the price for losing that loyalty.
Plus, for most people copying the AI funnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:04.480
to make money… it’s so saturated,&nbsp;
most don’t actually make money.&nbsp;

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:40.800
What a waste of everyone’s time.
With this video, I’m not saying to not use Etsy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:46.240
there are still great sellers there.
But, be careful when you shop online.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:52.080
AI can be a great tool, but a lot of products&nbsp;
feel like they’re getting worse because of it.&nbsp;

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:55.943
One of them… is Windows.
Microsoft pushed their AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.943 --> 00:19:01.920
CoPilot into about every possible part&nbsp;
of Windows they could, and it backfired.&nbsp;

